      },
      "class_row_html": "<tr>\n<td class=\"num\">14</td>\n<td>\n<a href=\"/abilities/paladin-healing-touch-i\">Healing Touch I</a>\n</td>\n<td class=\"muted\"></td>\n<td class=\"num muted\">\n              108\n            </td>\n<td class=\"muted\">2.5</td>\n<td class=\"num muted\">30</td>\n<td class=\"muted\">Heals your defensive target for 461.</td>\n</tr>",
      "detail_url": "https://vgsoharchive.com/abilities/paladin-healing-touch-i",
      "detail_cache": {
        "path": ".cache/archive/0dab27a7d455156b0b76a4adf236c75fe9eb293add6076d44adc843429c1adb4.txt",
        "sha256": "76da9bae889ad54ba46ea589dc7a9b2e1c5a746f64e5048cc3e364285c8031c1"
      },
      "detail_main_html": "<main class=\"wrap\">\n<div class=\"detail-head\">\n<h1>\n    \n    Healing Touch I\n  </h1>\n<p class=\"muted\">\n<a href=\"/classes/paladin\">Paladin</a>\n    \n    · Level 14\n    \n    \n  </p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"cols\">\n<div>\n<h2>Effect</h2>\n<div class=\"tooltip\">Heals your defensive target for 461.</div>\n<p class=\"muted small figure-note\">\n        Damage, healing and hate in Vanguard scale with your stats, skills and\n        level — the figures above are the ability's own, not what a\n        particular character will see.\n      </p>\n<h2>Notes</h2>\n<p class=\"muted\">The Cleric has a Healing Touch of its own, and it is a different ability rather than the same one shared. Compared at matching levels the Cleric's heals for more every time -- 23% more at rank I, narrowing to 10% by rank V -- which fits the Paladin being the heavier-armoured, lesser-healing half of the pair.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Energy efficiency differs between the two classes by a near-constant factor. Healing per point of energy spent runs 1.9 to 2.0 times better on the Paladin than on the Cleric at every matching level -- the Paladin heals less per cast, as expected, but costs less than half as much energy to do it. A ratio that steady across five ranks looks deliberate rather than accidental, but it is worth confirming which side carries the intended numbers.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Read from the in-game tooltip in VGO Emulator. Bracketed damage figures shown in game are the skill- and level-adjusted values for that character and are not recorded here.</p>\n</div>\n<div>\n<h2>Details</h2>\n<dl class=\"kv\">\n<div><dt>Level</dt><dd>14</dd></div>\n<div><dt>energy cost</dt><dd>108</dd></div>\n<div><dt>Cast time</dt><dd>2.5</dd></div>\n<div><dt>Range</dt><dd>30m</dd></div>\n<div><dt>Target</dt><dd>Defensive Target</dd></div>\n<div><dt>Type</dt><dd>Alteration</dd></div>\n</dl>\n<h2>Sources</h2>\n<ul class=\"plain\">\n<li><strong>Verified from the in-game tooltip</strong>\n<span class=\"muted\">— these figures override the wikis</span></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n</div>\n<p style=\"margin-top:26px\"><a href=\"/abilities\">← All abilities</a></p>\n</main>",
